(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff EP6002_0002_EX: Extended 2-channel serial interface EtherCAT Box with diagnostics.
</summary>
<description>
Extends EP6002_0002 with EtherCAT Working Counter, slave state, and CoE mailbox ADS address diagnostics.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
WcState=TRUE means process-data exchange is invalid. State is acyclic EtherCAT/link information,
not proof of current measurement validity. Link diagnostics to the matching slave InfoData entries.
The selected PDO representation is documented by the base terminal model.
InputToggle signals an input update by changing state; TRUE alone does not mean fresh data.
AdsAddr is acyclic mailbox addressing information, not a measurement-validity indicator.
Select the 22-byte serial payload with 16-bit status/control words; larger buffers and 9-bit modes
are outside this model. The owning service implements the transmit/receive toggle handshake.
</description>
*)
TYPE EP6002_0002_EX EXTENDS EP6002_0002 :
STRUCT
	WcState AT %I* : BOOL;
	InputToggle AT %I* : BOOL;
	State AT %I* : UINT;
	AdsAddr AT %I* : Global.AMSADDR;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>